---
import BasicLayout from '@/layouts/BasicLayout.astro';
---

<BasicLayout title="Terms of Service | Encode Edge" description="Terms of service and usage guidelines for Encode Edge.">
  <div class="mb-8 border-b pb-6">
    <span class="woords_tag_small mb-3">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl text-foreground tracking-tight">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-2">Last updated: September 2026</p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
  <p>
    By accessing and using Encode Edge ("the Site"), you accept and agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree with these terms, please do not use the Site.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Educational Content & Code Examples</h2>
  <p>
    All tutorials, code snippets, notebooks, and architectural guides provided on Encode Edge are for educational and informational purposes. While we strive for accuracy, code is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind. You are free to adapt code examples for your own learning and personal or commercial projects.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Intellectual Property</h2>
  <p>
    The original written articles, curriculum designs, brand assets, and custom illustrations on this site are protected by copyright and intellectual property laws.
  </p>

  <h2>4. User Conduct</h2>
  <p>
    You agree not to use the Site to distribute malicious code, scrape data excessively, or disrupt the operation of the platform.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Changes to Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We reserve the right to modify these terms at any time. Continued use of the Site following updates constitutes your acceptance of the revised terms.
  </p>
</BasicLayout>

